msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks/extracted-outputs/29965ec1-0fea-4162-9fbf-8af972d8c76c-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 2: Demonstrate non-Markovian error checks on a QPU and compare postselection strategies {#part-2-demonstrate-non-markovian-error-checks-on-a-qpu-and-compare-postselection-strategies}"
msgstr "Part 2: Ipakita ang non-Markovian error checks sa isang QPU at ihambing ang mga postselection strategy {#part-2-demonstrate-non-markovian-error-checks-on-a-qpu-and-compare-postselection-strategies}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that you have an understanding of what non-Markovian error checks are and how they are implemented in software, you can run a larger example on a QPU and see how it works.\n"
"First, prepare a circuit. The choice of circuit isn't very important; you only need a circuit for which you can easily verify the output. Here we choose a 20-qubit, 1D mirrored Ising circuit. This circuit is non-trivial to execute on hardware and should be affected by non-Markovian errors, which provides the opportunity to demonstrate the effectiveness of the non-Markovian error checks. Also, the mirrored structure allows us to trivially compare the noisy expectation value calculations against exact values.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayong naiintindihan mo na kung ano ang non-Markovian error checks at kung paano ito ipinapatupad sa software, puwede ka nang magpatakbo ng mas malaking halimbawa sa isang QPU at makita kung paano ito gumagana.\n"
"Una, maghanda ng circuit. Hindi gaanong mahalaga ang pagpili ng circuit; kailangan mo lang ng circuit na madaling i-verify ang output. Dito, pumili tayo ng 20-qubit, 1D mirrored Ising circuit. Hindi madaling i-execute ang circuit na ito sa hardware at dapat itong maapektuhan ng non-Markovian errors, kaya may pagkakataon tayong ipakita ang bisa ng non-Markovian error checks. Dahil din sa mirrored na istruktura, madali nating maihahambing ang mga noisy na kalkulasyon ng expectation value sa mga eksaktong halaga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this experiment, we are calculating observable expectation values. The choice of observable $O$ isn't important either, so we simply choose the average single-site magnetization $O=\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_i\\langle Z_i\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Sa eksperimentong ito, kinakalkula natin ang mga expectation value ng observable. Hindi rin mahalaga ang pagpili ng observable $O$, kaya pinili lang natin ang average na single-site magnetization $O=\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_i\\langle Z_i\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks/extracted-outputs/04f01a93-874c-4b95-bfb9-8e29caa7eaff-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks/extracted-outputs/04f01a93-874c-4b95-bfb9-8e29caa7eaff-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we add pre- and post-circuit checks on every qubit, including the seven adjacent spectator qubits. When you add all possible checks to a circuit, you can decide which postselection strategy to use during postprocessing.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, magdaragdag tayo ng mga check bago at pagkatapos ng circuit sa bawat qubit, kasama ang pitong katabing spectator qubit. Kapag naidagdag mo na ang lahat ng posibleng check sa isang circuit, puwede kang magpasya kung aling postselection strategy ang gagamitin sa postprocessing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the ``Executor`` primitive to sample the circuit containing the checks.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang ``Executor`` primitive para mag-sample ng circuit na may mga check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ``PostSelector`` class knows about the `creg` structure of the checks, so it can associate each bit in the samples to its associated circuit measurement. Its `compute_mask` method can be used to create a mask over a sequence of samples, given the postselection strategy (node or edge) and the type of non-Markovian error checks to look at (pre- or post-circuit). To combine pre- and post-circuit strategies into a single mask, their masks can be calculated independently and then combined with the ``AND`` operation. Here we use the ``PostSelector`` to create masks for all of the various strategies and look at the results using every permutation of strategies available.\n"
msgstr "Alam ng ``PostSelector`` class ang istruktura ng `creg` ng mga check, kaya kaya nitong iugnay ang bawat bit sa mga sample sa kaukulang circuit measurement nito. Ang `compute_mask` method nito ay magagamit para gumawa ng mask sa isang sequence ng mga sample, ayon sa postselection strategy (node o edge) at sa uri ng non-Markovian error checks na titingnan (pre- o post-circuit). Para pagsamahin ang pre- at post-circuit strategy sa iisang mask, puwedeng kalkulahin nang hiwalay ang mga mask nila at pagkatapos ay pagsamahin gamit ang ``AND`` operation. Dito, ginagamit natin ang ``PostSelector`` para gumawa ng mga mask para sa lahat ng iba't ibang strategy at tingnan ang mga resulta gamit ang bawat posibleng permutation ng mga available na strategy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the visualization below, we see how postselection strategy affects postselection rate, as well as the quality of answer. As expected, the strategies involving node-based postselection resulted in the lowest postselection rates. The edge-based strategies are more lenient and tend to result in higher postselection rates. Users should experiment with the various strategies on their problem to determine the right balance between postselection rate and quality of sampled distribution. In this example, using node-based postselection with the pre- and post-circuit checks resulted in the best answer with a postselection rate of ``.028%``. Some of the strategies did not outperform the raw circuit. You can also see that adding the checks but not using any of them (bar labeled \"no selection\" in chart below) performs the worst.\n"
msgstr "Sa visualization sa ibaba, makikita natin kung paano naaapektuhan ng postselection strategy ang postselection rate, pati na ang kalidad ng sagot. Gaya ng inaasahan, ang mga strategy na gumagamit ng node-based postselection ang nagresulta sa pinakamababang postselection rate. Mas maluwag ang mga edge-based na strategy at karaniwang nagreresulta sa mas mataas na postselection rate. Dapat subukan ng mga user ang iba't ibang strategy sa kanilang problema para matukoy ang tamang balanse sa pagitan ng postselection rate at kalidad ng na-sample na distribution. Sa halimbawang ito, ang paggamit ng node-based postselection kasama ang pre- at post-circuit checks ang nagbigay ng pinakamahusay na sagot na may postselection rate na ``.028%``. May ilang strategy na hindi nakahigit sa raw circuit. Makikita mo rin na ang pagdaragdag ng mga check nang hindi gumagamit ng alinman sa mga ito (ang bar na may label na \"no selection\" sa chart sa ibaba) ang pinakamasama ang performance.\n"

